WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.030
April 2013.

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.970
The Rana Plaza factory building
collapses in Bangladesh.

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.130
On 15 May, over 40 companies, two global
unions and eight Bangladeshi unions sign

4
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.010
an Accord on Fire and Building Safety.

5
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:19.290
More than 220 brands and
retailers later join.

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.290
Independent inspectors start
going into the factories.

7
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:27.310
Almost nine years on, how many
factories had fixed every problem found?

8
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.550
Almost all?

9
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.310
None?

10
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.010
In this mission, you'll place
company promises on a spectrum,

11
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.990
from voluntary codes to binding law.

12
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.230
Then you'll follow European
Union law from 2024 to 2026,

13
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.870
and read the Accord's
inspection data with care.

14
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.510
Your mission: find out how many
factories had fixed every problem found,

15
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.050
almost nine years on.
